From 1c88ceb5d557239d2b9a6cd717fdd9f5056c908a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] arm64: lld: place Clang CFI jump tables in core text

With CONFIG_LTO_CLANG, Clang 11 emits CFI jump tables in input sections
named .text..L.cfi.jumptable and .text..L.cfi.jumptable.*.  The existing
TEXT_MAIN and TEXT_CFI_MAIN patterns do not match the double-dot suffix,
so LLD leaves 26,362 jump-table sections as orphans before the output
.text, i.e. before _stext.  CONFIG_DEBUG_NOTIFIERS then rejects notifier
callbacks pointing at those entries (func_ptr_is_kernel_text() only
accepts _stext.._etext), skipping cpu_pm and other callbacks on every
idle transition.

Collect the jump-table sections explicitly into .text, the same
collection rule upstream uses in TEXT_CFI_JT (cf. commit 13b056696291
"vmlinux.lds.h: CFI: Reduce alignment of jump-table to function
alignment").  CFI stays enabled.

Verified on the built Image: all 26,362 CFI jump-table symbols are
inside _stext.._etext and the notifier-block relocations resolve to
in-range tables.
---
 include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h b/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
index 86351bae90f3..842289188461 100644
--- a/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
+++ b/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
@@ -465,6 +465,7 @@
 		*(.text..refcount)					\
 		*(.text..ftrace)					\
 		*(TEXT_CFI_MAIN) 					\
+		*(.text..L.cfi.jumptable .text..L.cfi.jumptable.*) \
 		*(.ref.text)						\
 	MEM_KEEP(init.text)						\
 	MEM_KEEP(exit.text)						\
